      "description": "Watch ADO Den Haag vs Groningen highlights and goals from Eredivisie on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 16, 2026. The Bingoal Stadion provided the perfect backdrop for a high-stakes Eredivisie encounter as both sides took to the pitch looking to assert their dominance. With tactical battles unfolding across every inch of the grass, the match promised a compelling narrative of perseverance and skill. Groningen takes command The visitors struck first blood in the 15th minute when Thom van Bergen coolly finished with his left foot to silence the home crowd. Despite an audacious bicycle-kick attempt from ADO Den Haag forward Yannick Eduardo , it was FC Groningen who surged further ahead. On the half-hour mark, Brynjolfur Andersen Willumsson slotted home a well-worked goal assisted by Etienne Vaessen , which was confirmed after a tense VAR check. Just before the interval on August 16, 2026, David van der Werff added a third goal to put the visitors in a commanding position heading into the break. A resilient fightback cut short Refusing to fold, ADO Den Haag emerged from the locker room with renewed purpose. Their persistence paid off in the 55th minute when Yannick Eduardo converted a left-footed strike following a creative pass from Finn de Bruin . While the home side increased their possession and pushed to narrow the gap, FC Groningen remained defensively disciplined. The outcome was firmly settled in the 81st minute, when Nils Eggens headed home a goal assisted by van Bergen . Despite a flurry of tactical substitutions and late efforts, the ADO Den Haag rally fell short as the visitors secured a decisive victory."
